According to the passage, what was the benefit of the silt left by the flood?', '["It stopped water from seeping away.", "It acted as a natural fertiliser.", "It removed salt from the soil.", "It helped engineers build barrages."]', 1, 'The passage calls the silt ''a free fertiliser''.', '{"0": "The passage says nothing about silt stopping seepage.", "2": "Salt comes later, with canals; silt is not said to remove it.", "3": "Barrages are not linked to the silt."}'),
  ('NEN-0003', 'Reading and figurative language', 'Inference', 'hard', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'Read the passage and answer the question.
