What can be inferred about land that was made fertile by irrigation?', '["Its fertility may not last if water is badly managed.", "It will always remain more fertile than flooded land.", "It never had any salt in it.", "It needs no further engineering."]', 0, 'The passage says such land ''can, after a few decades, become too salty to farm'', so its fertility can be lost.', '{"1": "The passage says it can become too salty to farm.", "2": "Salt builds up over time; nothing says it had none.", "3": "The final sentence calls for better engineering."}'),
