Why did makers of early pedal bicycles enlarge the front wheel?', '["A larger wheel was safer on stony roads.", "A larger wheel made the bicycle go faster with each turn of the pedals.", "It made room for a chain.", "Riders preferred to sit high above the road."]', 1, 'With pedals fixed to the front wheel, a bigger wheel covered more ground for each pedal turn: ''to go faster makers simply enlarged that wheel''.', '{"0": "The passage says high-wheelers were dangerous on stony roads.", "2": "The chain came later and made big wheels unnecessary.", "3": "Riders'' preferences are not given as the reason."}'),
  ('NEN-0013', 'Reading and figurative language', 'Inference', 'hard', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'Read the passage and answer the question.
