Why could the ''safety bicycle'' have two small wheels of equal size?', '["Small wheels were cheaper to make.", "Air-filled tyres needed small wheels.", "Riders no longer wanted to go fast.", "Gears and a chain, not wheel size, now set the speed."]', 3, 'The passage says that with the chain drive ''speed no longer depended on wheel size''.', '{"0": "Cost is not mentioned.", "1": "Tyres smoothed rough roads; they are not linked to wheel size.", "2": "Speed still mattered; it just came from the gears."}'),
  ('NEN-0014', 'Reading and figurative language', 'Organisation', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'Read the passage and answer the question.
