Which piece of evidence in the passage argues that the brain would not be mostly idle?', '["It is about two per cent of body weight.", "It uses about a fifth of the body''s energy.", "The myth is appealing.", "Simple tasks are easy."]', 1, 'An organ so costly to run would hardly have evolved if most of it did nothing.', '{"0": "Weight alone says nothing about use; it matters only beside the energy figure.", "2": "Appeal explains why the myth survives, not whether it is true.", "3": "The passage says simple tasks activate the whole brain, not that they are easy."}'),
  ('NEN-0023', 'Reading and figurative language', 'Inference', 'moderate', 'Markhor Prep original question', 'Read the passage and answer the question.
